BREAKING: agent registry stores HMAC-SHA-256 token hashes in config/agents.v2.json (registry_version 2) instead of plaintext tokens; set HAMMERTIME_INGEST_AGENT_TOKEN_KEY, convert the old file with `hammertime-agent-token migrate`, and repoint HAMMERTIME_INGEST_AGENTS_PATH before upgrading
Add `hammertime-agent-token` for generating agent tokens, writing their hashes into the registry, rotating a credential with a bounded overlap window (previous_token_hash plus a required expiry), and migrating a v1 plaintext registry
Add optional `attributes` to HotIpAdded/HotIpRemoved events, validated against schemas/ip_attributes.v1.json (registered names attributes_version/weight, x_-prefixed experimental keys, 1024-byte/16-key caps); absent attributes encode byte-identically to before
Add `weight_function` and `weight_max` config keys to detection_config, reserved for the fixed-point weight a future aggregator change will write into an IP's attributes at HOT/COLD transition
Reject observations whose sequence exceeds 9223372036854775807
Ingest claims an observation's (agent_id, sequence) atomically before publishing it, closing a race where concurrent retries of the same request could all be accepted; a retry after a 503 publish failure is now reported as a duplicate (200) rather than retried immediately, until the claim's dedup window lapses
BREAKING: event envelopes carry an optional `subject` that participates in event_id derivation; builds without it reject such envelopes as event_id mismatches
Ingest publishes accepted observations to hammertime.observations.v1 as one message per IP, keyed by that IP, returning 503 if publishing fails and 202 only once all of them are durably recorded; repeated IPs within one message are summed
Add ingest service: POST /v1/observations validates against schemas/observation.v1.json, rejecting malformed IPs, unaligned window_start, and oversized bodies/observation arrays with 400/413; accepted requests return 202 but are not yet published (no dedup/bus/auth wiring). Add GET /healthz liveness check and a placeholder GET /metrics
Add in-memory and Kafka-backed message bus (Producer/Consumer) with a canonical topic registry (hammertime.hot-ip.v1, observations, observations-reconciliation, prefix-stats), keyed by IP except prefix-stats which is keyed by prefix
Add event envelope and JSON codec for RequestObservation/HotIpAdded/HotIpRemoved/PrefixStatsChanged, with a deterministic event_id derived from (agent_id, sequence, event_type) for idempotent redelivery
